      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Tinea</h3>
          <p>Tinea is the name of a group of diseases caused by a fungus. Types include ringworm, athlete's foot and jock itch.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Eczema</h3>
          <p>Eczema is a term for a group of medical conditions that cause the skin to become inflamed or irritated. The most common type is atopic dermatitis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Urticaria</h3>
          <p>Also known as hives — an outbreak of swollen, pale red bumps or plaques (wheals) on the skin that appear suddenly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Vitiligo</h3>
          <p>Vitiligo (leukoderma / safed daag) is a common skin condition in India characterized by white patches on the skin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Wart</h3>
          <p>Warts are small, round, elevated non-cancerous skin growths that affect the topmost layer of the skin, caused by a virus.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Scabies</h3>
          <p>A contagious, intensely itchy skin condition caused by a tiny burrowing mite — spreads quickly within a family.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-card">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Pemphigus</h3>
          <p>A rare skin disorder characterized by blistering of the skin. There are two main types: Vulgaris and Foliaceus.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
